531
00:36:12,462 --> 00:36:13,714
You killed my husband.

532
00:36:13,797 --> 00:36:15,007
- Ging.
- Joel's gone!

533
00:36:15,090 --> 00:36:17,885
You killed my husband!
You killed my husband!

534
00:36:17,968 --> 00:36:19,428
He killed my husband!

535
00:36:19,511 --> 00:36:22,222
You killed my husband!
You killed my husband!

536
00:36:22,306 --> 00:36:23,891
I know you killed my husband!

537
00:36:33,775 --> 00:36:34,943
How is she?

538
00:36:35,027 --> 00:36:36,069
Calm.

539
00:36:40,365 --> 00:36:41,366
She's okay.

540
00:36:42,492 --> 00:36:44,745
But Ana, like I said...

541
00:36:46,204 --> 00:36:48,040
she needs to be admitted, okay?

542
00:36:50,334 --> 00:36:51,418
Yeah.

543
00:37:03,305 --> 00:37:04,640
Wait, wait, Auntie.

544
00:37:04,723 --> 00:37:06,391
Let's go over this again, okay?

545
00:37:06,475 --> 00:37:08,518
You received money,

546
00:37:08,602 --> 00:37:10,812
and you said it came from Angel?

547
00:37:11,355 --> 00:37:13,857
<i>Yes.</i>
<i>Why don't you believe me?</i>

548
00:37:14,441 --> 00:37:18,695
Because, Auntie,
we still haven't found Angel.

549
00:37:18,779 --> 00:37:23,742
Well, no one else sends money
to this phone except Angel.

550
00:37:23,825 --> 00:37:26,495
No one else knows my online wallet.

551
00:37:27,496 --> 00:37:29,331
Are you sure about that, Auntie?

552
00:37:29,414 --> 00:37:30,874
It could be a scam.

553
00:37:30,958 --> 00:37:31,959
Really?

554
00:37:32,042 --> 00:37:33,877
Then why hasn't anyone called me?

555
00:37:33,961 --> 00:37:36,046
I've had the money for days.

556
00:37:36,546 --> 00:37:38,882
That's why I called the sender myself.

557
00:37:39,466 --> 00:37:40,550
What did they say?

558
00:37:40,634 --> 00:37:42,803
<i>I asked where they were.</i>

559
00:37:42,886 --> 00:37:46,181
<i>They just said, "Abismo Compound."</i>

560
00:37:46,264 --> 00:37:49,184
<i>- Maybe Angel's there.</i>
- All right, Auntie.

561
00:37:49,685 --> 00:37:50,852
Thank you.

562
00:37:55,482 --> 00:37:57,317
Should I believe this?

563
00:37:59,820 --> 00:38:00,904
Angel...

564
00:38:05,200 --> 00:38:07,119
Hey! Everyone, wake up!

565
00:38:07,577 --> 00:38:10,080
Wake up! Wake up! Wake up!

566
00:38:10,163 --> 00:38:11,915
Hey! Wake up!

567
00:38:11,999 --> 00:38:13,417
Wake up!

568
00:38:14,501 --> 00:38:15,711
I said wake up!

569
00:38:15,794 --> 00:38:17,212
Wake up!

570
00:38:26,430 --> 00:38:28,515
What? You think you can escape?

571
00:38:29,307 --> 00:38:31,727
No! No...

572
00:38:31,810 --> 00:38:34,021
I just sent money to my mother.

573
00:38:34,104 --> 00:38:35,564
Then why did you run?

574
00:38:36,440 --> 00:38:38,025
Because you were chasing me.

575
00:38:40,360 --> 00:38:42,195
Get out! Move!

576
00:38:43,113 --> 00:38:44,197
Hurry!

577
00:38:50,078 --> 00:38:52,247
- No! No!
- What do you want?

578
00:38:52,831 --> 00:38:54,833
- No! No!
- Here. This one's pretty.

579
00:38:54,916 --> 00:38:56,376
It's not pretty! I don't want it!

580
00:38:56,460 --> 00:38:58,045
- It is pretty!
- What's going on?

581
00:38:58,128 --> 00:38:59,963
- What's going on?
- I don't want it!

582
00:39:00,047 --> 00:39:00,922
Regina?

583
00:39:01,006 --> 00:39:02,799
We're trying to find her
something else to wear,

584
00:39:02,883 --> 00:39:04,342
but she doesn't like
the clothes Ben bought.

585
00:39:04,426 --> 00:39:05,927
She says they all look the same.

586
00:39:07,179 --> 00:39:09,514
You don't like this?

587
00:39:11,475 --> 00:39:12,559
It's ugly, isn't it?

588
00:39:14,227 --> 00:39:15,562
Yeah, it's ugly.

589
00:39:16,480 --> 00:39:17,731
What do you want?

590
00:39:22,944 --> 00:39:24,613
You want something like this?

591
00:39:28,408 --> 00:39:29,993
I've got plenty of these.

592
00:39:30,994 --> 00:39:32,245
Let me see.

593
00:39:32,329 --> 00:39:34,164
- Here you go.
- It's so pretty!

594
00:39:34,706 --> 00:39:36,833
- Nanny, put it over here.
- Wow!

595
00:39:36,917 --> 00:39:38,085
Thank you.

596
00:39:43,757 --> 00:39:44,925
It's so pretty!

597
00:39:45,467 --> 00:39:46,551
Look!

598
00:39:46,635 --> 00:39:49,054
- Matching outfits?
- Now we're both pretty!

599
00:39:49,721 --> 00:39:51,139
It looks good on you.

600
00:39:51,223 --> 00:39:52,682
- Really?
- Mm.

601
00:39:53,266 --> 00:39:55,602
- Can I wear it?
- Do you want it?

602
00:39:55,685 --> 00:39:57,979
- Can I keep it?
- It's yours.

603
00:39:58,063 --> 00:39:59,147
Wow.

604
00:39:59,856 --> 00:40:01,108
It's so pretty!

605
00:40:03,110 --> 00:40:04,277
You're so nice.

606
00:40:05,112 --> 00:40:07,197
Maybe that's why my brother fell for you.

607
00:40:10,826 --> 00:40:13,829
What about you?
Why did you fall for my brother?

608
00:40:16,456 --> 00:40:18,125
There are so many reasons.

609
00:40:21,002 --> 00:40:22,337
Well...

610
00:40:22,420 --> 00:40:24,881
my brother's the smartest person
I've ever known.

611
00:40:28,718 --> 00:40:30,220
You two look so cute together.

612
00:40:32,806 --> 00:40:34,641
He used to teach me all the time.

613
00:40:34,724 --> 00:40:37,477
He'd always tell me,
"Ging, study hard, okay?

614
00:40:37,561 --> 00:40:40,564
You have to work hard
so we can get good jobs,

615
00:40:41,064 --> 00:40:42,607
so we won't go hungry."

616
00:40:42,691 --> 00:40:44,609
You know, we were always hungry back then.

617
00:40:44,693 --> 00:40:46,778
But I think my brother was even hungrier.

618
00:40:47,529 --> 00:40:51,366
Whenever he was about to take a bite,
he'd give it to me instead.

619
00:40:56,288 --> 00:40:58,915
Come on. Do you want to get changed?

620
00:40:59,499 --> 00:41:00,667
Come here.

621
00:41:17,601 --> 00:41:19,227
Eat your vegetables.

622
00:41:19,311 --> 00:41:21,062
- Ging, put your feet down.
- I don't want to.

623
00:41:21,146 --> 00:41:22,397
- Put your feet down.
- No!

624
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:24,149
- I'm comfortable like this.
- Sorry. Sorry I'm late.

625
00:41:24,232 --> 00:41:25,525
The food here is so good.

626
00:41:25,609 --> 00:41:27,611
You're not the only one eating.
Put your feet down.

627
00:41:27,694 --> 00:41:30,906
The food here is so good.
Mara and I ate the same thing every day.

628
00:41:36,494 --> 00:41:39,080
Ben, Ana, can't I just live here
with you?

629
00:41:41,291 --> 00:41:42,542
That's okay, right?

630
00:41:59,726 --> 00:42:01,728
That's so creepy.

631
00:42:02,145 --> 00:42:04,147
And I know creepy, so yes.

632
00:42:05,941 --> 00:42:06,942
What am I supposed to do?

633
00:42:07,025 --> 00:42:09,527
Do you think
I should just get the necklace...

634
00:42:09,611 --> 00:42:11,279
from her room or...

635
00:42:12,781 --> 00:42:13,949
I don't know.

636
00:42:14,658 --> 00:42:16,576
Isn't it obvious?

637
00:42:16,660 --> 00:42:18,954
Ben's sister needs to be admitted

638
00:42:19,037 --> 00:42:20,288
to a mental hospital.

639
00:42:20,372 --> 00:42:22,207
- Hey, press harder.
- Ma.

640
00:42:22,916 --> 00:42:24,000
What?

641
00:42:24,084 --> 00:42:26,253
I'm telling the truth.

642
00:42:26,336 --> 00:42:29,673
That woman is sick.
She belongs in a facility.

643
00:42:29,756 --> 00:42:32,175
Miss, what are you doing? Press harder.

644
00:42:32,259 --> 00:42:33,760
She's still Ben's sister.

645
00:42:35,679 --> 00:42:38,348
Actually, that's what Ben wants too.

646
00:42:39,557 --> 00:42:41,393
He wants to admit her.

647
00:42:43,478 --> 00:42:45,689
Then why don't you do it?

648
00:42:46,564 --> 00:42:47,691
Why?

649
00:42:48,733 --> 00:42:49,943
Well...

650
00:42:51,111 --> 00:42:54,114
there's such a stigma
around mental illness here in Vallente.

651
00:42:55,365 --> 00:42:57,617
If you don't want to send her
to a mental hospital,

652
00:42:57,701 --> 00:43:00,287
then bring her here instead.

653
00:43:00,370 --> 00:43:02,080
Let her stay here. I'll handle her.

654
00:43:02,163 --> 00:43:03,623
No.

655
00:43:03,707 --> 00:43:06,543
- What do you mean, no?
- I can't let that happen, Ma!

656
00:43:07,085 --> 00:43:09,879
You told me you weren't comfortable
with her staying there.

657
00:43:09,963 --> 00:43:11,464
But you don't want her to leave.

658
00:43:11,548 --> 00:43:14,718
And you don't want to admit her
because you feel sorry for her.

659
00:43:16,886 --> 00:43:18,471
There's only one thing left to do.

660
00:43:18,555 --> 00:43:20,307
All right, that's enough.

661
00:43:21,016 --> 00:43:22,017
Get out.

662
00:43:42,120 --> 00:43:43,913
- Here.
- Ma!

663
00:43:43,997 --> 00:43:45,290
I'm giving this to you.

664
00:43:45,373 --> 00:43:46,624
Take it home.

665
00:43:47,667 --> 00:43:48,835
No.

666
00:43:49,336 --> 00:43:50,754
What do you mean, no?

667
00:43:51,546 --> 00:43:53,548
She's not stable!

668
00:43:53,631 --> 00:43:56,468
One moment
she's trying on your clothes,

669
00:43:56,551 --> 00:43:59,304
after a minute,
she's lashing out on her brother.

670
00:43:59,387 --> 00:44:01,056
She even stole from you!

671
00:44:01,473 --> 00:44:03,058
She hasn't hurt me.

672
00:44:03,141 --> 00:44:04,476
Not yet.

673
00:44:04,934 --> 00:44:06,519
But what if Ben isn't around?

674
00:44:07,062 --> 00:44:08,730
What if she has another episode?

675
00:44:09,064 --> 00:44:12,067
She could end up killing you.

676
00:44:12,150 --> 00:44:14,194
Come on.

677
00:44:15,236 --> 00:44:16,905
If that time comes,

678
00:44:17,405 --> 00:44:20,575
it's better to have a gun than a knife.

679
00:45:03,785 --> 00:45:05,036
It's so white.

680
00:45:05,745 --> 00:45:06,996
So clean.

681
00:45:09,958 --> 00:45:12,127
When something's clean,
it's easy to stain.

682
00:45:14,671 --> 00:45:16,423
But once it's been stained,

683
00:45:17,048 --> 00:45:19,050
you can never restore it.

684
00:45:20,844 --> 00:45:23,263
It'll never be clean again.

685
00:45:27,642 --> 00:45:29,978
Joel used to tell me that.

686
00:45:30,854 --> 00:45:32,772
Every time I started painting.

687
00:45:37,360 --> 00:45:39,362
Now there's no one left to tell me.

688
00:45:45,034 --> 00:45:47,120
Because Ben killed my husband.

689
00:45:47,203 --> 00:45:49,122
Ben killed my husband.
Ben killed my husband.

690
00:45:49,205 --> 00:45:51,416
- He killed my husband!
- Regina! Regina!

691
00:45:55,086 --> 00:45:56,504
Did you see it?

692
00:46:01,926 --> 00:46:03,052
No.

693
00:46:03,928 --> 00:46:05,763
But I know he did it.

694
00:46:08,057 --> 00:46:09,309
How do you know?

695
00:46:11,311 --> 00:46:14,898
I just do! I know him.

696
00:46:15,356 --> 00:46:16,608
He's a murderer.

697
00:46:20,862 --> 00:46:22,447
Don't you believe me?

698
00:46:23,448 --> 00:46:25,283
Why? Because you think I'm crazy?

699
00:46:30,955 --> 00:46:32,874
Let's get some rest.

700
00:46:33,541 --> 00:46:36,377
Tomorrow, we'll go out.

701
00:46:39,964 --> 00:46:41,049
Okay.

702
00:47:41,192 --> 00:47:43,861
Attorney isn't here right now.
Do you have an ID?

703
00:47:43,945 --> 00:47:45,488
Ariel, who's that?

704
00:47:46,239 --> 00:47:47,240
Who's there?

705
00:47:47,323 --> 00:47:49,158
Someone's here
looking for Miss Ana.

706
00:47:53,413 --> 00:47:56,332
Why are you asking? Who are you?

707
00:47:59,002 --> 00:48:00,503
Is she here?

708
00:48:23,901 --> 00:48:26,571
I just really need to speak with her.

709
00:48:28,281 --> 00:48:31,200
I have something important to tell her.

710
00:48:31,284 --> 00:48:32,702
What's your name?

711
00:48:32,785 --> 00:48:34,495
So I can let her know.

712
00:48:34,579 --> 00:48:35,830
Tell me your name.

713
00:48:38,499 --> 00:48:39,584
Uh...

714
00:48:40,627 --> 00:48:42,962
I can only tell her.

715
00:48:43,713 --> 00:48:46,966
Please tell her it's really important.

716
00:48:47,383 --> 00:48:49,385
Could you please call her?

717
00:48:51,304 --> 00:48:52,555
Please call her.

718
00:48:53,139 --> 00:48:54,223
Keep an eye on her.

719
00:48:54,682 --> 00:48:57,101
Don't let her in until I get back.

720
00:48:57,185 --> 00:48:59,270
Please tell her it's important.

721
00:49:35,014 --> 00:49:36,683
<i>You're a monster!</i>

722
00:49:39,227 --> 00:49:40,687
Huh?

723
00:49:40,770 --> 00:49:42,271
Let me go!

724
00:49:43,940 --> 00:49:45,942
- You think I'm a nobody?
- No!

725
00:49:46,025 --> 00:49:49,153
- You didn't even save me a plate?
- No!

726
00:49:49,696 --> 00:49:51,114
Mom? Mom?

727
00:49:51,197 --> 00:49:56,244
Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom...

728
00:49:56,327 --> 00:49:57,829
No one should ever know about this.

729
00:49:58,329 --> 00:50:00,748
Hey! Keep it between us.

730
00:50:01,874 --> 00:50:04,460
Or else, I'll kill you too.

731
00:50:16,097 --> 00:50:17,682
<i>The monster is gone.</i>

732
00:50:19,183 --> 00:50:21,018
<i>No one will hurt us now.</i>

733
00:50:22,562 --> 00:50:24,397
<i>Tomorrow,</i>

734
00:50:25,022 --> 00:50:26,691
<i>we'll have a brand-new life.</i>

735
00:50:31,404 --> 00:50:33,072
We won't starve anymore.

736
00:50:33,906 --> 00:50:35,992
<i>We'll build a better life.</i>

737
00:50:36,075 --> 00:50:37,076
Whoo.

738
00:50:40,872 --> 00:50:43,166
- Here you go, boss.
- Hey.

739
00:50:43,249 --> 00:50:45,626
<i>Well, things are finally</i>
<i>looking up for you two.</i>

740
00:50:45,710 --> 00:50:46,544
<i>I hope so.</i>

741
00:50:47,462 --> 00:50:49,464
- Thank you.
- Ging, let's go.

742
00:50:49,547 --> 00:50:50,715
Ging?

743
00:50:52,091 --> 00:50:53,217
Gingging?

744
00:50:53,885 --> 00:50:54,886
Ging!

745
00:50:54,969 --> 00:50:56,053
Ging?

746
00:50:58,014 --> 00:50:58,848
Ging?

747
00:51:04,979 --> 00:51:05,980
Ging!

748
00:51:06,522 --> 00:51:08,983
- Ging! What's that?
- A burger.

749
00:51:09,066 --> 00:51:10,568
No, Ging. Spit it out.

750
00:51:10,651 --> 00:51:13,029
Spit it out! Come on. Spit it out.

751
00:51:14,280 --> 00:51:15,531
Ging...

752
00:51:16,699 --> 00:51:18,367
when I become a lawyer,

753
00:51:19,410 --> 00:51:21,579
I'll never let you go hungry again.

754
00:51:23,289 --> 00:51:25,374
I'll buy you a big house.

755
00:51:25,833 --> 00:51:27,084
And...

756
00:51:28,711 --> 00:51:32,048
we'll get you treated, okay?

757
00:51:32,757 --> 00:51:36,219
<i>Benjamin Santos,</i>
<i>you're under arrest for fraud.</i>

758
00:51:36,302 --> 00:51:38,221
<i>You have the right to remain silent.</i>

759
00:51:38,304 --> 00:51:40,807
<i>Anything you say may be used as evidence</i>

760
00:51:40,890 --> 00:51:42,850
<i>- against you in a court of law.</i>
- You can't take my brother!

761
00:51:42,934 --> 00:51:44,685
- He didn't do anything!
- Ging!

762
00:51:44,769 --> 00:51:45,978
- Ging!
- Let me go!

763
00:51:46,062 --> 00:51:47,980
- Sir, wait! Ging, look at me!
- Let me go!

764
00:51:48,064 --> 00:51:49,273
Ben!

765
00:51:49,357 --> 00:51:51,317
You're going to be a lawyer, right?

766
00:51:51,943 --> 00:51:54,362
Defend yourself!

767
00:51:54,445 --> 00:51:56,030
- Ben!
- Hold her! Hold her!

768
00:51:56,113 --> 00:51:58,115
Ben, no!

769
00:51:58,199 --> 00:52:01,202
- Ging! Ging!
- Let me go! Ben!

770
00:52:01,869 --> 00:52:04,789
No! Let me go! Ben!

771
00:52:06,707 --> 00:52:10,002
Ben! Come back! Ben!

772
00:52:10,711 --> 00:52:13,548
Damn it, Miss Berta.
I'm only asking one thing of you.

773
00:52:13,631 --> 00:52:15,508
Please don't neglect my sister.

774
00:52:16,008 --> 00:52:18,010
I'm paying you to take care of her.

775
00:52:18,094 --> 00:52:21,055
Come on, Ben.
Your sister's out of her mind.

776
00:52:21,138 --> 00:52:22,765
Just the other day,
while you were in jail,

777
00:52:22,849 --> 00:52:23,850
she went on a rampage here.

778
00:52:24,433 --> 00:52:27,019
We've done everything we could
to watch over her,

779
00:52:27,103 --> 00:52:29,647
but what can I do
when Regina isn't in her right mind?

780
00:52:29,730 --> 00:52:30,731
Ging?

781
00:52:34,986 --> 00:52:36,070
Ging?

782
00:52:40,366 --> 00:52:41,450
Ging!

783
00:52:47,248 --> 00:52:48,291
<i>Ging!</i>

784
00:52:49,959 --> 00:52:51,085
<i>Mara?</i>

785
00:52:51,586 --> 00:52:53,754
- That's enough.
- Mara!

786
00:52:54,547 --> 00:52:56,382
- I'm coming with him.
- Ging!

787
00:52:56,465 --> 00:52:58,384
- You can't go with him!
- I'm going with Joel!

788
00:52:58,467 --> 00:53:00,052
- I'm going with Joel!
- Wait, Regina!

789
00:53:00,136 --> 00:53:03,431
- She's coming with me.
- Ben... please don't get mad.

790
00:53:03,514 --> 00:53:06,183
It was me. This is all my fault.
Please don't get mad.

791
00:53:06,267 --> 00:53:07,935
She's stubborn.
That's why she got hurt.

792
00:53:08,019 --> 00:53:09,186
<i>Ben, it's me.</i>

793
00:53:09,854 --> 00:53:11,856
<i>Ben, please don't get mad.</i>
<i>Please don't get mad.</i>

794
00:53:11,939 --> 00:53:13,941
<i>- It was me, Ben. It's my fault.</i>
- <i>Shh...</i>

795
00:53:14,025 --> 00:53:15,151
<i>Please don't get mad.</i>

796
00:53:18,613 --> 00:53:22,033
<i>Ben, please. It was me.</i>
<i>This is all my fault.</i>

797
00:53:26,203 --> 00:53:28,456
- How about this...
- Ben, please.

798
00:53:28,539 --> 00:53:29,790
Shut up.

799
00:53:30,875 --> 00:53:32,293
Ten million.

800
00:53:32,376 --> 00:53:34,921
- So we can start over.
- Regina.

801
00:53:35,004 --> 00:53:36,130
Just ten million.

802
00:53:36,213 --> 00:53:37,632
- Right, Regina?
- Regina, please.

803
00:53:37,715 --> 00:53:39,133
We'll just leave, Ben.

804
00:53:39,216 --> 00:53:40,927
- We'll leave.
- Ging.

805
00:53:41,010 --> 00:53:42,470
Give us money.

806
00:53:42,553 --> 00:53:44,555
- Regina!
- Let's just leave.

807
00:53:44,639 --> 00:53:46,724
- Ten million.
- We'll just leave!

808
00:53:47,558 --> 00:53:49,060
She doesn't want to go.

809
00:53:49,143 --> 00:53:50,227
Go upstairs!

810
00:53:50,311 --> 00:53:53,898
- Go, Mara!
- Regina, stay here! Stay here!

811
00:53:55,358 --> 00:53:56,859
I know something about you.

812
00:53:58,361 --> 00:54:00,112
You'll love this.
I know something about you.

813
00:54:00,196 --> 00:54:01,405
No, don't.

814
00:54:01,489 --> 00:54:04,909
I remember every single story
Gingging told me.

815
00:54:04,992 --> 00:54:06,744
Don't say it!

816
00:54:06,827 --> 00:54:08,454
Ben, no. That's not true.

817
00:54:08,537 --> 00:54:09,747
About how you killed your father.

818
00:54:09,830 --> 00:54:11,290
- Don't! Don't say it!
- God damn it.

819
00:54:11,916 --> 00:54:13,584
- Don't say it!
- I know it's true.

820
00:54:13,668 --> 00:54:15,294
- Babe, stop.
- Attorney? What the hell?

821
00:54:15,378 --> 00:54:18,798
You killed your own father?
Do you want me to tell your wife?

822
00:54:19,423 --> 00:54:22,760
Attorney Benjamin Santos,
I'll keep my mouth shut...

823
00:54:23,469 --> 00:54:25,137
- for ten million.
- Babe, that's enough.

824
00:54:25,221 --> 00:54:27,515
- Hmm?
- Stop talking. Let's go, baby.

825
00:54:27,598 --> 00:54:29,600
Hold on. We're still talking.

826
00:54:32,770 --> 00:54:34,772
- Ben, no.
- Come on.

827
00:54:34,855 --> 00:54:36,273
Tomorrow.

828
00:54:36,357 --> 00:54:38,359
There we go! Now we're talking.

829
00:54:38,901 --> 00:54:40,653
This is easy.

830
00:54:40,736 --> 00:54:42,071
On one condition.

831
00:54:42,905 --> 00:54:46,075
My sister stays here.
Please. Is that okay?

832
00:54:46,158 --> 00:54:48,119
We're rich now, babe.

833
00:54:48,202 --> 00:54:50,788
- Joel, no.
- There you go.

834
00:54:50,871 --> 00:54:52,540
- Joel, no.
- Now that's better.

835
00:54:53,624 --> 00:54:56,460
- Ben...
- I'm leaving, Mara! It's all good.

836
00:54:56,919 --> 00:54:58,504
Joel, take me with you!

837
00:54:58,587 --> 00:55:00,756
Joel!

838
00:55:00,840 --> 00:55:03,050
Joel, take me with you!

839
00:55:03,134 --> 00:55:04,427
I'm out!

840
00:55:04,510 --> 00:55:06,178
- Let him go.
- Ben.

841
00:55:07,596 --> 00:55:09,348
Get some ice.

842
00:55:09,432 --> 00:55:11,642
Ice, Mara. Now.

843
00:55:15,312 --> 00:55:17,565
You're okay, Ging. Sit down.

844
00:55:17,648 --> 00:55:19,650
It's okay. Sit down.

845
00:55:19,734 --> 00:55:21,652
Okay. You're okay.

846
00:55:21,736 --> 00:55:23,988
You're okay.

847
00:55:24,739 --> 00:55:25,781
You're okay.

848
00:55:26,407 --> 00:55:28,659
Be gentle.

849
00:55:29,785 --> 00:55:32,913
Shh.

850
00:55:34,248 --> 00:55:36,000
That's enough.

851
00:55:36,083 --> 00:55:38,586
- He left me.
- He can't hurt you anymore.

852
00:55:40,463 --> 00:55:41,881
You're safe.

853
00:57:45,838 --> 00:57:47,673
She was right.

854
00:57:47,756 --> 00:57:49,341
Gingging was right.

855
00:57:50,009 --> 00:57:51,427
You're a monster!

856
00:58:42,770 --> 00:58:45,105
<i>If you don't want to do it,</i>
<i>don't do it.</i>

857
00:58:45,189 --> 00:58:47,608
<i>Because once you commit,</i>
<i>everything will change.</i>

858
00:58:47,691 --> 00:58:48,567
Ow!

859
00:58:48,651 --> 00:58:51,862
<i>Even the parts of you</i>
<i>that you're trying to protect.</i>

860
00:58:51,946 --> 00:58:53,030
Ana, you're scaring me.

861
00:58:53,113 --> 00:58:54,490

<i>Do you think love is the only thing</i>

862
00:58:54,573 --> 00:58:56,033
<i>that could drive a person mad?</i>

863
00:58:56,116 --> 00:58:58,702
<i>Sometimes, loneliness is far worse.</i>

864
00:58:58,786 --> 00:59:00,120
No!

865
00:59:00,204 --> 00:59:02,331
- What's happening? Wait!
Ana! Help me!

866
00:59:02,414 --> 00:59:03,499
Let her go!

867
00:59:03,582 --> 00:59:04,833
- No! Ana!
Let her go!

868
00:59:04,917 --> 00:59:09,046
Sure. He's a nice guy.
But he's done terrible things too.

869
00:59:09,129 --> 00:59:12,424
<i>Do you really think</i>
<i>you know everything about him?</i>

870
00:59:12,508 --> 00:59:13,676
Ana!

871
00:59:15,886 --> 00:59:17,429
I need to tell you the truth.

872
00:59:18,430 --> 00:59:19,640
Fuck you, Mara.

873
00:59:19,723 --> 00:59:22,476
A monster? You're a monster.
You're a monster!

874
00:59:22,559 --> 00:59:24,687
You're a monster! Get away from me!

875
00:59:24,770 --> 00:59:26,939
- <i>Get away from me!</i>
<i>Regina!</i>

876
00:59:28,649 --> 00:59:31,402
<i>You can still save yourself.</i>

877
00:59:31,485 --> 00:59:33,904

